    "note": "Direction terms are controlled. Translators/renderers must not freely substitute stronger or weaker safety direction words.",
    "patch_2026-08-28": "Orphan-recovery patch (see validate-formula-safety-reachability.js R2). A1(a)'s first pass fell back to needs_review whenever a segment did not literally match a pattern, which removed genuinely-safety-bearing sentences from the visible card when they used a near-synonym verb the original pattern lists happened not to list (e.g. 不宜長期服用 vs 不宜久服, do not take X in large doses vs avoid high-dose use). This patch adds near-synonym patterns for real orphaned corpus sentences only, verified against zero collisions in already-canonical text before adding (scripts/a1-safety-recover-orphans.js). It does not add any generic/bare verb pattern broad enough to risk misclassifying unrelated sentences (e.g. bare \"discontinue use\" or \"do not take\" were rejected in favor of the fuller literal phrase actually present in the corpus)."
  },
  "field_semantics": {
    "contraindications": {
      "decision_test_zh": "來源是否明確要求在該狀態下不得使用？",
      "decision_test_en": "Does the source explicitly require that the product not be used in the stated condition?",
      "meaning": "hard prohibition supported by source wording"
    },
    "cautions": {
      "decision_test_zh": "來源是否保留在監測、調整、專業評估或指定前提下仍可使用的可能？",
      "decision_test_en": "Does the source leave open the possibility of use after monitoring, adjustment, professional assessment, or a specified prerequisite?",
      "meaning": "conditional use, monitoring, adjustment, supervision, prerequisite, or nonclinical restriction"
    }
  },
